       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects could last for days.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **5 mg PO daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg PO daily**, which is sometimes used in frail patients or with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf 50 mg is correct, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll reconsider. I'd also suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
