      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review from here. No standard amlodipine protocol uses 50 mg once daily, and the dose is high enough to cause severe, prolonged hypotension and shock. That risk is too high for me to enter it on an unverified claim.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter it through pharmacy or your prescriber workflow.** The reviewing pharmacist can enter or co-sign the order, with the protocol referenced in the system. That creates the documentation and the verification that I can't provide.\n- **Send me a protocol reference.** If you give me the protocol name or document and the specifics, such as the target indication and the monitoring parameters, I'll reconsider. I still can't verify it myself, so I may still decline.\n- **Order a standard dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg PO daily right away, and you can titrate from there.\n\nIf the 50 mg is a typo, for example for 5 mg, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
